#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Introducción {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum "
"computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using "
"quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and "
"entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bits, puertas y circuitos son los componentes fundamentales de la "
"computación cuántica. Aprenderás computación cuántica con el modelo de "
"circuitos utilizando bits cuánticos y puertas, y además repasarás "
"superposición, medición y entrelazamiento.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"En esta lección aprenderás:\n"
"- Puertas de un solo qubit\n"
"- Esfera de Bloch\n"
"- Superposición\n"
"- Medición\n"
"- Puertas de dos qubits y estados entrelazados\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is "
"essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Al final de esta clase, aprenderás sobre la profundidad de circuito, que es "
"crucial para la computación cuántica a escala de utilidad.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. La computación como diagrama {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the "
"inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very"
" few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a "
"*circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cuando utilizamos qubits o bits, necesitamos manipularlos para convertir las"
" entradas existentes en las salidas necesarias. Para los programas más "
"sencillos con muy pocos bits, es útil representar este proceso en un "
"diagrama conocido como *diagrama de circuito*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-"
"right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs "
"are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are "
"represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called "
"“gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr ""
"La figura de abajo a la izquierda muestra un ejemplo de un circuito clásico,"
" y la figura de abajo a la derecha muestra un ejemplo de un circuito "
"cuántico. En ambos casos, las entradas están a la izquierda y las salidas a "
"la derecha, mientras que las operaciones se representan mediante símbolos. "
"Los símbolos utilizados para las operaciones se denominan \"puertas\" "
"principalmente por razones históricas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. Puerta cuántica de un solo qubit {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr ""
"3.1 Estado cuántico y esfera de Bloch {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and "
"$|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr ""
"El estado de un qubit se representa como una superposición de $|0\\rangle$ y"
" $|1\\rangle$. Un estado cuántico arbitrario se escribe como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that "
"$|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $\\alpha$ y $\\beta$ son números complejos tales que "
"$|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex "
"vector space:\n"
msgstr ""
"$|0\\rangle$ y $|1\\rangle$ son vectores en el espacio vectorial complejo "
"bidimensional:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, un estado cuántico arbitrario también se representa como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a "
"two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of "
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"De esto podemos ver que el estado de un bit cuántico es un vector unitario "
"en un espacio de producto interno complejo bidimensional con una base "
"ortonormal de $|0\\rangle$ y $|1\\rangle$. Está normalizado a 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ también se denomina vector de estado (statevector).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Un estado cuántico de un solo qubit también se representa como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the "
"following figure.\n"
msgstr ""
"donde $\\theta$ y $\\varphi$ son los ángulos de la esfera de Bloch en la "
"siguiente figura.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"En las siguientes celdas de código, construiremos cálculos básicos a partir de los componentes en Qiskit. Construiremos un circuito vacío y luego añadiremos operaciones cuánticas, discutiendo las puertas y visualizando sus efectos.\n"
"Puedes ejecutar la celda con \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Primero importa las bibliotecas.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Preparación del circuito cuántico {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Creamos y dibujamos un circuito de un solo qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
