#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3.3 Measurement {#33-measurement}"
msgstr "3.3 Medición {#33-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurement is theoretically a very complicated topic. But in practical terms, making a measurement along $z$ (as all IBM&reg; quantum computers do) simply forces the qubit’s state $\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle \\quad (s.t.|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1)$ either to $|0\\rangle$ or to $|1\\rangle,$ and we observe the outcome.\n"
"- $|\\alpha|^2$ is the probability we will get $|0\\rangle$ when we measure.\n"
"- $|\\beta|^2$ is the probability we will get $|1\\rangle$ when we measure.\n"
msgstr ""
"La medición es teóricamente un tema muy complicado. Pero en términos prácticos, una medición a lo largo de $z$ (como hacen todos los computadores cuánticos de IBM&reg;) simplemente fuerza el estado del qubit $\\alpha|0\\rangle+\\beta|1\\rangle \\quad (s.t.|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1)$ a $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle,$ y observamos el resultado.\n"
"- $|\\alpha|^2$ es la probabilidad de obtener $|0\\rangle$ al medir.\n"
"- $|\\beta|^2$ es la probabilidad de obtener $|1\\rangle$ al medir.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are called probability amplitudes. (see \"Born "
"rule\")\n"
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, $\\alpha$ y $\\beta$ se denominan amplitudes de probabilidad. "
"(ver \"regla de Born\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|1\\rangle$"
" has an equal probability of becoming $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ upon "
"measurement. $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}|0\\rangle-\\frac{1}{2}i|1\\rangle$ has a "
"75% chance of becoming $|0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por ejemplo, $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|1\\rangle$"
" tiene igual probabilidad de convertirse en $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle$ al "
"medir. $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}|0\\rangle-\\frac{1}{2}i|1\\rangle$ tiene un 75%"
" de probabilidad de convertirse en $|0\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Aer Simulator {#qiskit-aer-simulator}"
msgstr "Simulador Qiskit Aer {#qiskit-aer-simulator}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, let's measure a circuit that prepares the equal probability superposition above.\n"
"We should add the measurement gates, as the Qiskit Aer simulator simulates an ideal (with no noise) quantum hardware by default. Note: The Aer simulator can also apply a noise model based on real quantum computer. We will return to noise models later.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, medimos un circuito que prepara la superposición anterior con igual probabilidad.\n"
"Debemos añadir las puertas de medición, ya que el simulador Qiskit Aer simula por defecto hardware cuántico ideal (sin ruido). Nota: El simulador Aer también puede aplicar un modelo de ruido basado en un computador cuántico real. Volveremos a los modelos de ruido más adelante.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/3956e602-9f1b-4083-b58d-26c91b50b75e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/3956e602-9f1b-4083-b58d-26c91b50b75e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We are now ready to run our circuit on the Aer simulator. In this example, "
"we will apply the default shots=1024, which means we will measure 1024 "
"times. Then we will plot those counts in a histogram.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora estamos listos para ejecutar nuestro circuito en el simulador Aer. En "
"este ejemplo usamos la configuración predeterminada shots=1024, lo que "
"significa que medimos 1024 veces. Luego representamos estos conteos en un "
"histograma.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/7cb7c5ab-7b12-4f77-aaca-1d7e6cff213c-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/7cb7c5ab-7b12-4f77-aaca-1d7e6cff213c-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that 0s and 1s were measured with a probability of almost 50% each. "
"Although noise has not been simulated here, the states are still "
"probabilistic. So while we expect roughly a 50-50 distribution, we will "
"rarely find exactly that. Just as 100 flips of a coin would rarely yield "
"exactly 50 instances of each side.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vemos que los 0s y 1s se midieron cada uno con una probabilidad de casi el "
"50%. Aunque no se simuló ruido aquí, los estados siguen siendo "
"probabilísticos. Aunque esperamos aproximadamente una distribución 50-50, "
"rara vez la encontraremos exactamente. Al igual que 100 lanzamientos de "
"moneda rara vez darán exactamente 50 instancias de cada lado.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
